 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "A variable-entered map for f(A, B, C) uses only A and B as map variables. Each cell holds what f is as a function of the entered variable C for that A, B: 0, 1, C or C′.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n0",
     "set": {
      "text": "cell = f(A, B, C) as a function of C"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Unfold it: each VEM cell becomes two cells of the full map, C = 0 and C = 1. Cell A = 0, B = 0 holds C, so f(0, 0, 0) = 0 and f(0, 0, 1) = 1; cell A = 0, B = 1 holds 1, so both are 1; cell A = 1, B = 0 holds 0; cell A = 1, B = 1 holds C′, so only C = 0 gives 1.",
   "patches": [
